-- title:
--   Eq. (20) — for t large and â_t near a⁽⁰⁾, the CVP price is within |TI(t)| of p(â_t) (index corrected)
-- statement:
--   Assume (3) has at most one root and fix the CVP parameters $\alpha$, $c$. There are $\rho > 0$ and $t_0$ such that for every $t \ge t_0$ and every price/demand path that follows Controlled Variance Pricing: if the MQLE $\hat a_t$ exists and $\|\hat a_t - a^{(0)}\| \le \rho$, then
--
--   $$|p_{t+1} - p(\hat a_t)| \le |\mathrm{TI}(t)| = 2\sqrt{c[(t+1)^\alpha - t^\alpha]\tfrac{t+1}{t}}, \tag{20}$$
--
--   where $|\mathrm{TI}(t)|$ is the length of the taboo interval.
--
--   Either the policy charges the certainty equivalent price $p(\hat a_t)$, or that price lies in the taboo interval and the policy moves to the nearest admissible maximizer, which sits on the boundary of $\mathrm{TI}(t)$. The pricing error therefore splits into an estimation part and a taboo-interval part of order $t^{(\alpha-1)/2}$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The page prints $|p_t - p(\hat a_t)| \le |\mathrm{TI}(t)|$ "for all $t > T_\rho$", having said just before that $t$ must be sufficiently large. The price set from $\hat a_t$ and $\mathrm{TI}(t)$ is $p_{t+1}$, and "$t$ sufficiently large" is the explicit threshold $t_0$. The statement is deterministic: it concerns every path generated by the rule.
-- source:
--   den Boer, Zwart, Simultaneously Learning and Optimizing Using Controlled Variance Pricing, Management Science 60(3):770–783 (2014), p. 782 (PDF 14), proof of Theorem 1, eq. (20)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_KeskinZeevi_SufficientConditions_LeastSquares
import Definitions.Def_CVPricing_Regret_Model
import Definitions.Def_CVPricing_Regret_CVP

open KeskinZeevi.SufficientConditions

namespace CVPricing.Regret

/-- Eq. (20) (den Boer–Zwart 2014, proof of Theorem 1, p. 782), with the index corrected: there are
`ρ > 0` and `t₀` such that for every `t ≥ t₀` and every price/demand path that follows CVP, if the
MQLE `â_t` satisfies `‖â_t − a⁽⁰⁾‖ ≤ ρ`, then the next price obeys
`|p_{t+1} − p(â_t)| ≤ |TI(t)| = 2√(c[(t+1)^α − t^α](t+1)/t)`. The page prints `|p_t − p(â_t)|` "for
all `t > T_ρ`"; the price set from `â_t` and `TI(t)` is `p_{t+1}`, and the text requires `t`
sufficiently large. Uses the disclosed uniqueness of the MQLE. -/
theorem price_near_optimum_taboo (M : Model) (hU : MQLEUnique M) (α c : ℝ) :
    ∃ ρ : ℝ, 0 < ρ ∧ ∃ t₀ : ℕ, ∀ t : ℕ, t₀ ≤ t → ∀ p d : ℕ → ℝ, IsCVPPath M α c p d →
      ∀ a, IsMQLE M p d t a → euclidNorm (a - M.a0) ≤ ρ →
        |p (t + 1) - optPriceOf M a| ≤ 2 * tabooHalfWidth α c t := by sorry

end CVPricing.Regret
